
Topic: LibreOffice Calc Interface

Objective:
To study the LibreOffice Calc interface and identify its basic components.

Result:
The interface of LibreOffice Calc was successfully studied and all major components were identified.

Important Components:
• Title Bar
• Menu Bar
• Standard Toolbar
• Formatting Toolbar
• Formula Bar
• Name Box
• Worksheet Area
• Rows
• Columns
• Cells
• Sheet Tabs
• Status Bar


Title:

To Study the LibreOffice Calc Interface

Procedure

Step 1:
Click the Start Menu and open LibreOffice Calc.

Step 2:
Wait until the main worksheet appears on the screen.

Step 3:
Observe the Title Bar, which displays the file name.

Step 4:
Identify the Menu Bar containing options such as File, Edit, View, Insert, Format, Sheet, Data, Tools, Window, and Help.

Step 5:
Observe the Standard Toolbar, which provides quick access to common commands.

Step 6:
Identify the Formatting Toolbar used to change fonts, alignment, colors, borders, and other formatting options.

Step 7:
Locate the Formula Bar, where formulas and cell contents are displayed.

Step 8:
Identify the Name Box, which displays the address of the currently selected cell.

Step 9:
Observe the Worksheet Area, consisting of rows, columns, and cells.

Step 10:
Locate the Sheet Tabs at the bottom used to manage multiple worksheets.

Step 11:
Observe the Status Bar, which displays information such as the current mode, selected data summary, and zoom level.

Step 12:
Close LibreOffice Calc after completing the observation.